<li class=3D"toclevel-1 tocsection-45 toc-level-1"><a href=3D"https://www.l=
imesurvey.org/manual/Question_types#Styling_questions"><span class=3D"tocnu=
mber">3</span> <span class=3D"toctext">Styling questions</span></a></li>
</ul>
</div>

<p><br>
</p>
<h1><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Introduction">Introduction</span></h1=
>
<p>This page offers you a visual overview of all available question types. =
You can also see it as a starting point from where you can get to different=
 wiki sections that explain in detail every question type.
</p>
<div class=3D"simplebox"><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"=
><a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:Help.png" class=3D"mw-fi=
le-description"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/a/aa/H=
elp.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"25" height=3D"25" class=3D"mw-file-ele=
ment"></a></span> The LimeSurvey download package includes a sample survey =
which includes all question types. You'll find it in your "/docs/demosurvey=
s/" directory. Import each of them and try every question type!</div>
<p>Please note that a LimeSurvey survey consists of question groups which c=
ontain one or more question. Therefore, you must <b>create a question group=
 first</b> before you add questions to your survey. For more details on que=
stion groups, read the following <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manu=
al/Question_groups_-_introduction" title=3D"Question groups - introduction"=
>wiki section</a>.
</p>
<h1><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Question_types">Question types</span>=
</h1>
<p>To change the question type, you must first open the question in <i>edit=
 mode</i> and click the <b>General options</b> tab located in the panel on =
the right side of the page:
</p><p><br>
</p>
<center><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https=
://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:Question_type_button_location.png" class=
=3D"mw-file-description"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/imag=
es/2/2d/Question_type_button_location.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"1525=
" height=3D"466" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a></span></center>
<p><br>
Then, select the desired question type from the <i>Select question type</i>=
 menu.  To help ensure that you choose the correct question type, a preview=
 of the question type is displayed in the <i>Select question type</i> panel=
.=20
</p><p><br>
</p>
<center><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https=
://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:Question_type_-_2.png" class=3D"mw-file-d=
escription"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/5/5d/Quest=
ion_type_-_2.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"888" height=3D"559" class=3D"=
mw-file-element"></a></span></center>
<p><br>
</p>
<div class=3D"simplebox"><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"=
><a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:Help.png" class=3D"mw-fi=
le-description"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/a/aa/H=
elp.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"25" height=3D"25" class=3D"mw-file-ele=
ment"></a></span>Check our <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Que=
stions_-_introduction" title=3D"Questions - introduction">introduction on q=
uestions</a> section for more information</div>
<p><br>
</p>
<hr width=3D"50%" style=3D"margin:auto">
<p><br>
The following question styles can be used within a survey in LimeSurvey:
</p>
<ul><li><a class=3D"mw-selflink-fragment" href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.or=
g/manual/Question_types#Arrays">Arrays</a></li>
<li><a class=3D"mw-selflink-fragment" href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/ma=
nual/Question_types#Mask_questions">Mask questions</a></li>
<li><a class=3D"mw-selflink-fragment" href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/ma=
nual/Question_types#Multiple_choice_questions">Multiple choice questions</a=
></li>
<li><a class=3D"mw-selflink-fragment" href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/ma=
nual/Question_types#Single_choice_questions">Single choice questions</a></l=
i>
<li><a class=3D"mw-selflink-fragment" href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/ma=
nual/Question_types#Text_questions">Text questions</a></li></ul>
<p><br>
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Subquestions">Subquestions</span></h3=
>
<p>Usually a question only has answers. But there are certain question type=
s (like the Array question type) which are basically a subset of questions =
where each subquestion can be answered by the survey participant (often by =
using a predefined scale of answer options).
</p><p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https:=
//www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:F_AFL.png" class=3D"mw-file-description"><=
img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/4/4e/F_AFL.png" decodin=
g=3D"async" width=3D"1153" height=3D"253" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a></s=
pan>
</p><p>A more complex example is the question type 'Array of texts' where t=
he respondent has to enter values for combinations. In that case the value =
entered by the respondent is the 'answer' and the two scales on the array a=
re two scales of subquestions.
</p><p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https:=
//www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:SC_MFT.png" class=3D"mw-file-description">=
<img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/3/31/SC_MFT.png" decod=
ing=3D"async" width=3D"1149" height=3D"294" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a><=
/span>
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Arrays">Arrays</span></h2>
<p>The <i>Array question type</i> further extends the <i>List question type=
</i>. Using this question type, a matrix can be displayed where the left co=
lumn is represented by a subquestion, while each row is represented by the =
same set of answer options. The text of the question can be either a specif=
ic question or a description.
</p><p>In terms of output there is no difference in how responses are store=
d compared to <i>List (Radio)</i> question type. The given answer is stored=
 in a separate column in the result table for both question types.
</p><p>The most flexible array types are <i>Array</i>, <i>Array (Text)</i> =
and <i>Array (Numbers)'. However, LimeSurvey also supports a number of arra=
y types which have predefined answer options (e.g., </i>Array 5 point choic=
e<i>).</i>
</p>
<div class=3D"simplebox"> <span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File=
"><a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:Help.png" class=3D"mw-f=
ile-description"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/a/aa/=
Help.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"25" height=3D"25" class=3D"mw-file-el=
ement"></a></span> To quickly understand the basics of array-type questions=
, check the following <a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer noope=
ner" class=3D"external text" href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3D7134=
QebOQzY">video tutorial</a>.</div>=20
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Array">Array</span></h3>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;translate&gt;
</div>
<p>An array allows you to create a set of <a class=3D"mw-selflink-fragment"=
 href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_types#Subquestions">sub=
questions</a>. Each of them uses the same set of answer options. For exampl=
e, you can use this question type when you need feedback on several aspects=
 of a particular product.
</p>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;/translate&gt;</div>
<p><b>Example 1:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/a/=
aa/Question_tpye_-_Array_using_flexible_labels.zip" class=3D"internal" titl=
e=3D"Question tpye - Array using flexible labels.zip">Question type - Array=
 using flexible labels.zip</a>
</p><p><b>Example 2:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/image=
s/3/3b/Question_type_-_Array_-_Semantic_Differential_Question_Type.zip" cla=
ss=3D"internal" title=3D"Question type - Array - Semantic Differential Ques=
tion Type.zip">Question type - Array - Semantic Differential Question Type.=
zip</a>
</p><p>Find out <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_=
-_Array" title=3D"Question type - Array">more about the Array question type=
...</a>
</p>
<h3><span id=3D"Array_.285_point_choice.29"></span><span class=3D"mw-headli=
ne" id=3D"Array_(5_point_choice)">Array (5 point choice)</span></h3>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;translate&gt;
</div>
<p>It is an array type that is prefilled with answer choices. An 1 to 5 sca=
le is used. A "No answer" answer option is automatically added if the quest=
ion is not mandatory.
</p>
<div class=3D"simplebox"><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"=
><a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:Help.png" class=3D"mw-fi=
le-description"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/a/aa/H=
elp.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"25" height=3D"25" class=3D"mw-file-ele=
ment"></a></span> <b>Hint:</b> If you need scales other than 5 points, use =
the general <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Ar=
ray" title=3D"Question type - Array">array question type</a>. </div>
<p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://ww=
w.limesurvey.org/manual/File:A-5_point.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description"><=
img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/2/27/A-5_point.jpg" dec=
oding=3D"async" width=3D"1153" height=3D"253" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a=
></span>
</p><p><br>
<b>Example:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/0/09/Ar=
ray_5_point_choice_example.zip" class=3D"internal" title=3D"Array 5 point c=
hoice example.zip">Array 5 point choice example.zip</a>
</p>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;/translate&gt;</div>
<p>Find out <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Ar=
ray_(5_point_choice)" title=3D"Question type - Array (5 point choice)">more=
 about the 5 Point Choice Array question type...</a>
</p>
<h3><span id=3D"Array_.2810_point_choice.29"></span><span class=3D"mw-headl=
ine" id=3D"Array_(10_point_choice)">Array (10 point choice)</span></h3>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;translate&gt;
</div>
<p>It is an array question type that is prefilled with answer choices on a =
1 to 10 scale. A "No answer" answer option is automatically added if the qu=
estion is not mandatory.
</p>
<div class=3D"simplebox"><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"=
><a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:Help.png" class=3D"mw-fi=
le-description"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/a/aa/H=
elp.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"25" height=3D"25" class=3D"mw-file-ele=
ment"></a></span> <b>Hint:</b> If you need to use another scale, change the=
 question type to the general <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/=
Question_type_-_Array" title=3D"Question type - Array">array question type<=
/a>. </div>
<p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://ww=
w.limesurvey.org/manual/File:B_10_point.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description">=
<img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/a/ab/B_10_point.jpg" d=
ecoding=3D"async" width=3D"1146" height=3D"266" class=3D"mw-file-element"><=
/a></span>
</p><p><b>Example:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/=
8/84/Array_10_point_choice_example.zip" class=3D"internal" title=3D"Array 1=
0 point choice example.zip">Array 10 point choice example.zip</a>
</p>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;/translate&gt;</div>
<p>Find out <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Ar=
ray_(10_point_choice)" title=3D"Question type - Array (10 point choice)">mo=
re about the 10 Point Choice Array question type...</a>
</p>
<h3><span id=3D"Array_.28Yes.2FNo.2FUncertain.29"></span><span class=3D"mw-=
headline" id=3D"Array_(Yes/No/Uncertain)">Array (Yes/No/Uncertain)</span></=
h3>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;translate&gt;
</div>
<p>It is an array question type that is prefilled with the following answer=
 choices: "Yes", "No", and "Uncertain". You can also add a "No answer" choi=
ce if the question is not mandatory.
</p><p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https:=
//www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:C_YNU.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description"><=
img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/b/b1/C_YNU.jpg" decodin=
g=3D"async" width=3D"1144" height=3D"248" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a></s=
pan>
</p><p><br>
<b>Example:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/a/a9/Ar=
ray_Yes_No_Uncertain_Example.zip" class=3D"internal" title=3D"Array Yes No =
Uncertain Example.zip">Array Yes No Uncertain Example.zip</a>
</p>
<div class=3D"simplebox"><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"=
><a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:Help.png" class=3D"mw-fi=
le-description"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/a/aa/H=
elp.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"25" height=3D"25" class=3D"mw-file-ele=
ment"></a></span> The "No answer" option is displayed if the question is <b=
>not</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Array=
_(Yes-No-Uncertain)#Mandatory" title=3D"Question type - Array (Yes-No-Uncer=
tain)">mandatory</a>.</div>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;/translate&gt;</div>
<p>Find out <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Ar=
ray_(Yes-No-Uncertain)" title=3D"Question type - Array (Yes-No-Uncertain)">=
more about the Yes/No/Uncertain Array question type...</a>
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h3><span id=3D"Array_.28Increase.2FSame.2FDecrease.29"></span><span class=
=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Array_(Increase/Same/Decrease)">Array (Increase/Same=
/Decrease)</span></h3>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;translate&gt;
</div>
<p>It is an array type that is prefilled with the following answer choices:=
 "Increase", "Same", and "Decrease". A "No answer" answer option is automat=
ically added if the question is set to be not mandatory.=20
</p><p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https:=
//www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:E_ISD.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description"><=
img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/5/58/E_ISD.jpg" decodin=
g=3D"async" width=3D"1146" height=3D"246" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a></s=
pan>
</p><p><b>Example:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/=
6/6d/Array_increase_decrease_example.zip" class=3D"internal" title=3D"Array=
 increase decrease example.zip">Array increase decrease example.zip</a>
</p>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;/translate&gt;</div>
<p>Find out <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Ar=
ray_(Increase-Same-Decrease)" title=3D"Question type - Array (Increase-Same=
-Decrease)">more about the Increase/Same/Decrease Array question type...</a=
>
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Array_by_column">Array by column</spa=
n></h3>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;translate&gt;
</div>
<p>This question type is the same as an array, except the subquestion and a=
nswer axes are swapped.
</p><p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https:=
//www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:H_AFL_BC.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description=
"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/0/0e/H_AFL_BC.jpg" d=
ecoding=3D"async" width=3D"1146" height=3D"350" class=3D"mw-file-element"><=
/a></span>
</p><p><br>
<b>Example:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/2/21/Ar=
ray_by_column_example.zip" class=3D"internal" title=3D"Array by column exam=
ple.zip">Array by column example.zip</a>
</p>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;/translate&gt;</div>
<p>Find out <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Ar=
ray_by_column" title=3D"Question type - Array by column">more about the Arr=
ay by Column question type...</a>
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Array_dual_scale">Array dual scale</s=
pan></h3>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;translate&gt;
</div>
<p>This question type provides two scales of answer options for each subque=
stion. A heading can be set for each scale from the <a href=3D"https://www.=
limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Array_dual_scale#Display" title=3D"Qu=
estion type - Array dual scale">question display options</a>:
</p><p><br>
<span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://www.l=
imesurvey.org/manual/File:1_DSC.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description"><img src=
=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/2/2a/1_DSC.jpg" decoding=3D"as=
ync" width=3D"1150" height=3D"285" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a></span>
</p><p><br>
You can also set a special question attribute to use this question type wit=
h dropdown boxes:
</p><p><br>
<span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://www.l=
imesurvey.org/manual/File:1_DSC_DD.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description"><img =
src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/1/11/1_DSC_DD.jpg" decoding=
=3D"async" width=3D"1152" height=3D"238" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a></sp=
an>
</p><p><br>
<b>Example 1:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/5/50/=
Dual_Scale_Example.zip" class=3D"internal" title=3D"Dual Scale Example.zip"=
>Dual Scale Example.zip</a>
</p><p><b>Example 2:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/image=
s/d/da/Dual_Scale_Dropdown_Example.zip" class=3D"internal" title=3D"Dual Sc=
ale Dropdown Example.zip">Dual Scale Dropdown Example.zip</a>
</p>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;/translate&gt;</div>
<p>Find out <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Ar=
ray_dual_scale" title=3D"Question type - Array dual scale">more about the A=
rray Dual Scale question type...</a>
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h3><span id=3D"Array_.28Numbers.29"></span><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=
=3D"Array_(Numbers)">Array (Numbers)</span></h3>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;translate&gt;
</div>
<p>This question types allows survey administrators to a create large array=
s with numbered dropdown boxes with a set of subquestions on the "y-axis", =
and another set of subquestions on the "x-axis".
</p><p><br>
</p>
<center><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https=
://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:DP_MFN.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description"=
><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/8/83/DP_MFN.jpg" deco=
ding=3D"async" width=3D"1153" height=3D"290" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a>=
</span></center>
<p>You can also set a <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question=
_type_-_Array_(Numbers)#Checkbox_layout_(multiflexible_checkbox)" title=3D"=
Question type - Array (Numbers)">special question attribute</a> to use this=
 question type with checkboxes:
</p><p><br>
</p>
<center><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https=
://www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:DP_MFN_CB.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-descripti=
on"><img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/f/f2/DP_MFN_CB.jpg=
" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"1149" height=3D"292" class=3D"mw-file-element=
"></a></span></center>
<p><br>
<b>Example 1:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/0/07/=
Example_Array_Numbers.zip" class=3D"internal" title=3D"Example Array Number=
s.zip">Example_Array_Numbers</a>
</p><p><b>Example 2:</b> <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/image=
s/3/38/Example_Array_Numbers_Checkboxes.zip" class=3D"internal" title=3D"Ex=
ample Array Numbers Checkboxes.zip">Example_Array_Numbers_Checkboxes</a>
</p>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;/translate&gt;</div>
<p>Find out <a href=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/Question_type_-_Ar=
ray_(Numbers)" title=3D"Question type - Array (Numbers)">more about the num=
bers Array question type...</a>
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h3><span id=3D"Array_.28Texts.29"></span><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D=
"Array_(Texts)">Array (Texts)</span></h3>
<div style=3D"display:none;">&lt;translate&gt;
</div>
<p>The Array (Text) question type allows for an array of text boxes with a =
set of subquestions as the "y-axis", and another set of subquestions as the=
 "x-axis".
</p><p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https:=
//www.limesurvey.org/manual/File:SC_MFT.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description">=
<img src=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/images/0/06/SC_MFT.jpg" decod=
